# TODO

- Make a default prefix for content hash tags, like basil-<hash> instead of just <hash>

## Known gaps

- `RUN --mount=type=ssh` is a hard error (buildah run has no ssh mount, so the
  agent cannot be forwarded).
- Imperative `COPY .` copies per-file (dockerignore-honest, dest-reconstructed):
  a very large context becomes many `buildah copy` calls. Batching or a
  filtered tar stream (`buildah add -`) is the future optimization.
- `IMPORT` of a local stage name (inline another target's own layers) is
  rejected at closure time with a clear error — `COPY --from=<stage>` is the
  current way to pull a stage's content into a layer.
- `FROM --platform=<other $VAR>` (anything but $BUILDPLATFORM/$TARGETPLATFORM):
  unexpandable selectors are a hard error; the two build-staged vars expand to
  the host platform.
- IMPORT inlines the import image's flattened content as one new layer; the
  import's original layer digests are not re-added, and its config
  (ENV/CMD/...) is not transferred (`IMPORT` is content-only).
- `COMMIT` checkpoints are local-only (the buildah layer cache, group
  granularity): probed with `buildah inspect` and resumed with `buildah from`
  — one local probe per checkpoint per run; a local-first registry-adjacent
  store could make them survive `buildah rmi` cleanup, but they are also
  cheaply re-sealed on demand.